---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { filled, site } from '../config/site';

// Keep this in step with the code: retention periods are enforced by the daily job in src/lib/jobs.ts,
// and the providers listed are the ones the site actually calls.
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and protects your personal information when you book or get in touch.`}
  updated="2026-10-27"
  intro="This explains what personal information we collect when you book or get in touch, what we do with it, who we share it with and how long we keep it."
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} is the controller of your personal information. We're registered in England and Wales{
      filled(site.companyNumber) && `, company no. ${site.companyNumber}`
    }{filled(site.registeredOffice) && `, at ${site.registeredOffice}`}.{
      filled(site.icoNumber) && ` We're registered with the Information Commissioner's Office, registration number ${site.icoNumber}.`
    }
  </p>
  <p>Questions about your information go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you book</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, email address and mobile number.</li>
    <li>Your dates, number of guests, the extras you choose and the price.</li>
    <li>Anything else you tell us: estimated arrival time, a note, and your company name if it's a work trip.</li>
    <li>
      When you ticked the box to accept the booking terms and house rules, which version you accepted, and the IP address you booked
      from. We keep this as a record of what you agreed to.
    </li>
    <li>
      Whether you have paid and any refund. Stripe takes your card details on its own form, so we never see or store them. We only see
      the payment status and a payment reference.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When you send an enquiry</h3>
  <p>
    Your name, email address, phone number if you give it, and what you tell us: dates, number of guests, company, the purpose of the stay,
    whether you need an invoice and your message.
  </p>

  <h3>When you contact us directly</h3>
  <p>Emails and WhatsApp messages you send us, and our replies.</p>

  <h3>When you use the website</h3>
  <p>
    Cloudflare, which hosts the site, processes your IP address and browser details to deliver pages and protect the site from attacks.
    We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which doesn't use cookies and doesn't identify you. The site also records booking
    steps (such as a price being shown or a checkout being opened) without any personal details, so we can see how the booking process is
    working. See the <a href="/cookies">cookie notice</a> for what is stored in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it, and our legal basis</h2>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">What we do</th><th scope="col">Legal basis</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            Take your booking and payment, add it to our booking calendar, send your confirmation, arrival details and other emails about
            your stay, handle cancellations and refunds
          </td>
          <td>Performing our contract with you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Reply to your enquiry and send you a quote</td>
          <td>Taking steps at your request before a contract, or our legitimate interest in answering questions about our homes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Keep booking and payment records</td>
          <td>Legal obligation (company and tax law)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Keep a record of the terms you accepted, deal with damage or disputes</td>
          <td>Our legitimate interest in protecting our business and the homes we look after</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Check forms for spam and bots, keep the website secure</td>
          <td>Our legitimate interest in running a safe website</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>After your stay, send one thank-you email with a way to book with us again</td>
          <td>Our legitimate interest in welcoming guests back. Tell us and we won't send it</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>We don't sell your information, use it for advertising or make automated decisions about you.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We use these providers to run the site and our bookings. Each only gets what it needs to do its job.</p>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">What for</th><th scope="col">Where</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Stripe</td><td>Taking payments and refunds, and preventing fraud</td><td>UK, EU and US</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Website hosting, the booking database, spam checks on forms (Turnstile) and visit counts</td><td>Global network, US company</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Sending booking and enquiry emails</td><td>US</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Smoobu</td><td>Our booking calendar, which keeps every booking site in step</td><td>EU (German company)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Zoho Mail</td><td>Our email inbox</td><td>Zoho's EU or US data centres</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Slack</td><td>Alerts to the hosts about new bookings and enquiries (name, dates and number of guests)</td><td>US</td></tr>
        <tr><td>WhatsApp (Meta)</td><td>Messages, only if you message us there</td><td>US and other countries</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Stripe also uses payment information for its own fraud checks, as a separate controller under its own privacy policy. We may also
    share information with our insurer if there is a claim, with professional advisers, or with the police or other authorities where the
    law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Transfers outside the UK</h2>
  <p>
    Some of these providers handle information in the US or elsewhere outside the UK. Where they do, the transfer is covered by UK
    adequacy rules (including the UK extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework) or by the UK's approved contract clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Paid bookings:</strong> seven years after your stay, which covers the six years company and tax law ask for.</li>
    <li><strong>Bookings that were never paid, and withdrawn requests:</strong> 12 months.</li>
    <li><strong>Enquiries through the website:</strong> 12 months. If an enquiry becomes a booking, the booking record is kept as above.</li>
    <li><strong>Emails and messages:</strong> as long as we need them to deal with your stay or any question about it, then deleted.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Deleting old bookings and enquiries happens automatically.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>give you a copy of the information we hold about you</li>
    <li>correct anything that's wrong</li>
    <li>delete your information, where we don't have to keep it</li>
    <li>limit how we use it, or stop using it for something based on our legitimate interests</li>
    <li>send it to you or another company in a common format</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We'll reply within one month. If you're not happy with how we've handled your
    information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a>
    or on 0303 123 1113. We'd appreciate the chance to sort it out first.
  </p>

  <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
  <p>
    The site runs over an encrypted connection, booking records are only open to the two of us, and card payments never reach our systems.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change how we use your information, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
</Legal>
